//! ## Key Content
//!
//! ### 1. Skies and Meta-Fractals
//!
//! The paper reframes high-dimensional Cayley-Dickson zero divisors as the basis
//! for scale-free "Sky" structures: infinite families of orthogonal ZD lines
//! organized by non-power-of-two strut constants.
//!
//! ### 2. Box-Kites as the Basic ZD Molecule
//!
//! Box-kites remain the core 16D building block. This revision emphasizes how
//! those octahedral ZD ensembles seed higher-dimensional emanation tables and
//! support the recursive bookkeeping used later in the Placeholder series.
//!
//! ### 3. Recipe-Style Construction Agenda
//!
//! Part I of the manuscript sets up the production rules, exclusion rules, and
//! bit-manipulation patterns used to generate larger ZD families. The later
//! placeholder installments then extend those recipes into explicit sky-building
//! and "recipe theory" workflows.
